--
N5008 [expr.prim.fold]/2, [temp.variadic]/5, [expr.sizeof]/1: in the
fold `(0 + ... + sizeof(xs))' each instantiated element is `sizeof(x_k)',
the size of the k-th element's type (1, 4 and 8 for char, int, double).
The front end computed a wrong value: the fold expansion substituted the
pack element only in positional sub-trees, and the operand of
`sizeof(xs)' is kept in the named type_arg (it parses as a type-id until
resolved).  test_type_pack.desc: the same over the TYPE pack.
Found while extending cpp17_pack_extended_by_deduction_after_explicit_arguments.
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept the program.  Fails on the round-163 build bin52.
